GPUI's macOS platform, gpui-pre-macos 0.3.9 as published (a snapshot of Zed at 93d7456), with the
changes Mu needs until a gpui-pre snapshot has them (zed-industries/zed#65472 or its like for the
first):

- A window's display link pauses once nothing has asked for a frame for 100 ms, so an idle window
  doesn't wake the main thread on every refresh of the display. GPUI's `frame_waker` and
  `schedule_frame` start it again (`window.rs`, with `request_frame_now` in `display_link.rs`).
- A drag Mu hands to macOS, like files dragged out to another app, stops the last mouse move being
  replayed once it begins (`draggingSession:willBeginAtPoint:` in `window.rs`).
- Its deprecation warnings are allowed, as Zed's workspace allows them and the published manifest
  leaves that out (`Cargo.toml`). Cargo shows a patched crate's warnings, unlike a crates.io one's.

